### 4.4 Runnable vs Callable vs Future — Side-by-Side Comparison

| Feature | `Runnable` | `Callable<V>` | `Future<V>` |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Package** | `java.lang` | `java.util.concurrent` | `java.util.concurrent` |
| **Since** | Java 1.0 | Java 5 | Java 5 |
| **Returns value** | ❌ No (`void`) | ✅ Yes (`V`) | ✅ Yes (via `get()`) |
| **Throws checked exception** | ❌ No | ✅ Yes | N/A |
| **Method name** | `run()` | `call()` | `get()`, `isDone()`, etc. |
| **Used with** | `execute()`, `submit()` | `submit()` | Returned by `submit()` |
| **Purpose** | Fire-and-forget task | Task with result | Handle to async result |

```java
// Summary of usage patterns:
ExecutorService ex = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(2);

// Runnable — no result
ex.execute(() -> System.out.println("Runnable"));

// Callable — has result
Future<Integer> f = ex.submit(() -> 42);

// Future — get the result later
int value = f.get(); // 42
```

