## 7. ScheduledExecutorService

Run tasks after a delay, or on a repeating schedule.

### 7.1 schedule() — Run Once After Delay

```java
import java.util.concurrent.*;

public class ScheduleOnceExample {

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {

        ScheduledExecutorService scheduler = Executors.newScheduledThreadPool(2);

        System.out.println("Scheduling task at: " + System.currentTimeMillis());

        // Run after a 3-second delay
        ScheduledFuture<String> future = scheduler.schedule(
            () -> "Task executed at: " + System.currentTimeMillis(),
            3,
            TimeUnit.SECONDS
        );

        System.out.println("Waiting for result...");
        System.out.println(future.get()); // blocks until task completes

        scheduler.shutdown();
    }
}
```

### 7.2 scheduleAtFixedRate() — Fixed Rate (Timer-like)

```java
import java.util.concurrent.*;
import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;

public class FixedRateExample {

    public static void main(String[] args) throws InterruptedException {

        ScheduledExecutorService scheduler = Executors.newScheduledThreadPool(1);
        AtomicInteger count = new AtomicInteger(0);

        // Start after 1s initial delay, then run every 2s
        // ⚠️ If task takes longer than period, next execution waits for it to finish
        ScheduledFuture<?> handle = scheduler.scheduleAtFixedRate(
            () -> System.out.println("Heartbeat #" + count.incrementAndGet()
                                     + " at " + System.currentTimeMillis()),
            1,       // initial delay
            2,       // period
            TimeUnit.SECONDS
        );

        Thread.sleep(9000); // Let it run 4 times
        handle.cancel(false); // Stop the task
        scheduler.shutdown();
    }
}
```

### 7.3 scheduleWithFixedDelay() — Fixed Delay Between Completions

```java
import java.util.concurrent.*;

public class FixedDelayExample {

    public static void main(String[] args) throws InterruptedException {

        ScheduledExecutorService scheduler = Executors.newScheduledThreadPool(1);

        // Wait 1s after COMPLETION of last run before starting next
        // ✅ Safer than fixedRate when tasks can be slow
        scheduler.scheduleWithFixedDelay(
            () -> {
                System.out.println("Poll DB at " + System.currentTimeMillis());
                try { Thread.sleep(500); } catch (InterruptedException e) { Thread.currentThread().interrupt(); }
            },
            0,      // start immediately
            2,      // wait 2s after each completion
            TimeUnit.SECONDS
        );

        Thread.sleep(10000);
        scheduler.shutdown();
    }
}
```

| Method | Timing | Use Case |
|---|---|---|
| `schedule()` | Once after delay | One-shot delayed task |
| `scheduleAtFixedRate()` | Every N ms from start | Metrics collection, heartbeats |
| `scheduleWithFixedDelay()` | N ms after last completion | Polling, retries |

