## 12. Quick Reference — Comparison Table

### Executor Factory Methods

| Method | Threads | Queue | keepAlive |
|---|---|---|---|
| `newFixedThreadPool(n)` | n | Unbounded LBQ | N/A |
| `newCachedThreadPool()` | 0–∞ | SynchronousQueue | 60s |
| `newSingleThreadExecutor()` | 1 | Unbounded LBQ | N/A |
| `newWorkStealingPool()` | CPU count | ForkJoin deque | N/A |
| `newScheduledThreadPool(n)` | n | DelayedWorkQueue | N/A |

### Runnable vs Callable vs Future

| | Runnable | Callable | Future |
|---|---|---|---|
| Returns value | No | Yes | Yes (via get()) |
| Throws checked ex | No | Yes | Wraps in ExecutionException |
| Method | run() | call() | get(), isDone(), cancel() |
| Used with | execute(), submit() | submit() | returned by submit() |

### Future vs CompletableFuture

| Feature | Future | CompletableFuture |
|---|---|---|
| Blocking get() | Yes | Optional |
| Chaining | ❌ | ✅ thenApply/thenCompose |
| Combine futures | ❌ | ✅ thenCombine/allOf/anyOf |
| Exception handling | awkward | ✅ exceptionally/handle |
| Manual completion | ❌ | ✅ complete(value) |
| Java version | 5 | 8 |

